{"title":"Career Roadmap · Process Engineer","role":"Process Engineer","summary":"A Process Engineer in the pulp, paper and coating industry is responsible for understanding, controlling, optimizing and improving industrial manufacturing processes.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Pulp, Paper & Coating Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Process Engineer in the pulp, paper and coating industry is responsible for understanding, controlling, optimizing and improving industrial manufacturing processes."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pulping technology"},{"text":"Paper manufacturing"},{"text":"Chemical processing"},{"text":"Mechanical and process engineering"},{"text":"Coating technology"},{"text":"Instrumentation and control"},{"text":"Quality management"},{"text":"Energy and water optimization"},{"text":"Process data analysis"},{"text":"Troubleshooting"},{"text":"Production improvement"},{"text":"Sustainability"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate profile should progress from understanding the complete pulp-to-paper process to process control, optimization, troubleshooting and data-driven manufacturing."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech/B.E. Pulp, Paper & Coating Technology","Engineering + Chemistry + Materials Fundamentals","Wood/Fiber Science + Pulping","Bleaching + Stock Preparation","Paper Machine Operations","Drying + Calendering + Finishing","Coating + Surface Treatment","Instrumentation + Process Control","Quality + Energy + Water Optimization","Process Data + Statistical Analysis","Industrial Internship / Plant Exposure","Graduate Process Engineer / Process Trainee","Process Engineer","Senior Process Engineer","Process Optimization / Production Specialist","Process Engineering Manager / Tec